\author{utensil}
\date{2026-08-02}

\p{These are the accompanying mathematical notes for the experimental research
project \href{https://github.com/utensil/fcap}{FCAP}. FCAP is read “F-cap,” and
studies whether Lean can serve both as a formal language for the abstract and
concrete mathematics of Clifford algebras and as an implementation language
for efficient symbolic and numerical computation. It is also a coined acronym
for “Formalized Clifford Algebra Programme.”}

\p{FCAP's formalization is still at an early spike-test stage. The main
storyline follows its own coordinate representations and orthogonal-product
transport. The appendix is a mathematical companion to Tau Ceti's Clifford
and Spin work: it connects the filtered exterior model, reflection and
Pin/Spin constructions, bivector lifts, real signatures, and spinor modules.
Those results supply context and possible tools for FCAP's longer program;
the appendix does not claim they are FCAP formalizations.}

